.TH SLML 1 "2026-10-26" "slml 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slml \- compiler for SLML, the Strict Layout Markup Language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slml
.IR file.slml ...
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.br
.B slml
.I folder
.RB [ \-o
.IR output-folder ]
.br
.B slml check
.IR file-or-folder ...
.br
.B slml serve
.RI [ folder ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-open ]
.br
.B slml view
.I file.slml
.br
.B slml render
.I file.slml
.RB [ \-o
.IR out.png ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slml
compiles SLML documents. Like a C compiler, it turns each input file into an
output file next to it:
.I page.slml
becomes
.IR page.html .
The shared stylesheet and the bundled fonts are written to a
.I _slml
folder in the site root.
.PP
Given a folder,
.B slml
builds a whole site: every page is compiled, files that only contain
.B style
and
.B define
(component libraries) are skipped, and every other file (images, downloads)
is copied. The default output folder is
.IR folder/_site .
.PP
Documents are checked strictly. Any error, including a link to a local file
that does not exist, is reported with its file, line and column, and no
output is written for that file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Only report errors. Folders are checked recursively.
.TP
.B serve
Start a preview web server on 127.0.0.1 (port 4000 or the next free one).
Pages are compiled on every request, errors are shown in the browser, and
open pages reload automatically when a file changes.
.TP
.B view
Open a file in the native SLML viewer (not available when built without the
.I viewer
feature).
.TP
.B render
Render a page to a PNG image with the native renderer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIpath\fR
Output file or folder. An output ending in
.I .png
is rendered as an image; anything else is HTML.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " folder"
Site root for paths that start with
.IR / .
Default: the current folder if the file is inside it, otherwise the file's
folder. When building a folder, the folder is the root.
.TP
.BI \-\-width " px"
Page width for PNG output (default 900).
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " n"
Pixel density for PNG output and the viewer (default 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " n"
First port to try for
.BR serve .
.TP
.B \-\-open
With
.BR serve ,
open the preview in the default browser.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only errors.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the compiler and language version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if any file has errors or cannot be written.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
slml index.slml
slml index.slml \-o public/index.html
slml site/ \-o public/
slml serve site/ \-\-open
slml check site/
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The SLML handbook (the
.I handbook
folder of the source repository) and
.IR SPEC.md .
